Using "twonum" is allowed in addition to (not replacing) twonum.org.

However, you are allowed to use this image inside of another work
without licensing it under CC BY-SA if it meets ALL of the following:
  - The entire work is used, unmodified, or the only modification are one or more of:
    - Resizing while preserving aspect ratio
      - This refers to resizing/rendering the image to make it have a
        higher/lower resolution, NOT cropping or distorting it in any way.
      - The image MUST NOT be resized to a resolution lower than
        88x31, or rendered to a resolution lower than 88x31.
      - Metadata is encouraged to be preserved.
    - Format shifting to another lossless format
      - This refers to converting the image to either SVG
        (preserving the pixel rendering)
        or to another lossless format, including
        BMP, GIF, TIFF, or another PNG.
      - The resulting image must match the pixels of the original PNG.
      - This does not include WebP or formats allowing both lossy and lossless,
        which are unpredictable.
  - The word "twonum" must be legible.
  - If the image or text in proximity is linked, or if used in an HTML document
    or a language that outputs HTML, it must lead directly, to one of:
    - https://www.twonum.org/
    - https://hub.twonum.org/
  - You are not impersonating twonum or disparaging her.
  - You are not hosting or operating a website claiming to be:
    (Note: Archival websites which link back to the original source,
    like web.archive.org, are allowed under this rule.)
    - twonum.org
    - DoubleFloat
    - hub.twonum
    - Pronums
  - You MUST NOT use the work or a derivative for any form of
    generative AI training or as input for any generative AI system.
    - Generative AI is defined as computer systems that outputs
      content such as images and text based on training data
      comprised of existing, copyrighted data.

("The work" refers to this image, the twonum.org button.)
